  "note": "Every circuit and layout in GT7, as the game lists them. This is the catalogue the event screen's track and layout pickers are built from. It replaces the 86-name string list in gt7_extra.json, which held 27 of the 41 circuits - Yas Marina, Suzuka, Mount Panorama, Interlagos, Laguna Seca, Brands Hatch and nine others were simply absent, and it spelt Eiger Nordwand 'Eiger Norwand'.",
  "source": "Gran Turismo Wiki, Gran Turismo 7/Track List - https://gran-turismo.fandom.com/wiki/Gran_Turismo_7/Track_List",
  "sourceRead": "2026-08-13",
  "why": "The same page and the same read date as gt7_track_weather.json, which is the point: the rain answer and the track list were two files that could disagree, and did. `rain` is carried here per layout so the two can be checked against each other.",
  "reverse": "`reversible` is GT7's own column. The picker offers a '(Reverse)' layout for each one. 84 layouts and 37 reversible make 121 configurations; the wiki's prose says 120, so one of the two is out by one. The per-row column is used, not the prose total.",
